[{:db/id "q-161566/selection/bb3e45981e3f443c7c33cc2e616b17442dd9c8089dad62194449f81483f69ef5" :answer/id #uuid "6433b86e-c036-56a1-95ce-759b9d4f6faa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{sin}^{2}⁡z+\\pi -8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161566/selection/2194c055d3d480bfe7c29b912a8a3e2e4b9b1b131fe5c4935c3f6e4a66795f38" :answer/id #uuid "561d8166-9d56-5672-8862-d9a312ad1674" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{sin}^{2}⁡z-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161566/selection/bd483da70c5a6cf7476774039b99cb668ea2482fd017ba0a9d3835949b716ed7" :answer/id #uuid "e8442034-9627-59f0-ad6b-e467f3306316" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}+2z-2y-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161566/selection/0f0847c8bb3149bb0bb57b52119e7f521a73da6fd02de25756048d4ab84c7a91" :answer/id #uuid "6a52495d-c609-55ee-84e8-757277db0d93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}+2z-2y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161566/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" :answer/id #uuid "373d34ce-61bb-5a3a-a3a6-fef504beeec4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161566/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "07b7ce3a-2397-54f6-a2d3-f73cacc91ccb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161566/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" :answer-field/choices ["q-161566/selection/bb3e45981e3f443c7c33cc2e616b17442dd9c8089dad62194449f81483f69ef5" "q-161566/selection/2194c055d3d480bfe7c29b912a8a3e2e4b9b1b131fe5c4935c3f6e4a66795f38" "q-161566/selection/bd483da70c5a6cf7476774039b99cb668ea2482fd017ba0a9d3835949b716ed7" "q-161566/selection/0f0847c8bb3149bb0bb57b52119e7f521a73da6fd02de25756048d4ab84c7a91" "q-161566/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161566" :question/id #uuid "52af5bc1-756d-5cea-af80-685583e8af64" :question/math-academy-id "q-161566" :question/problem "The triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz\n$$\n\nis defined over the type II region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-8\\le y\\le {sin}^{2}⁡z,\\,0\\le z\\le \\pi ,\\,-2y-1\\le x\\le {y}^{2}+2z}.\n$$\n\nWhat is $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "A type II region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {u}_{2}(y,z)}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/a905e1f60fb0aa865c071fcbccbfecb30dcac7a74b4b647d24a40f4c89ff1935.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type II region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(y,z)=-2y-1,\\,{u}_{2}(y,z)={y}^{2}+2z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-2y-1}^{{y}^{2}+2z}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA.\n$$\n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-8\\le y\\le {sin}^{2}⁡z,\\,0\\le z\\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-2y-1}^{{y}^{2}+2z}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{-8}^{{sin}^{2}⁡z}[{\\int }_{-2y-1}^{{y}^{2}+2z}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dy\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{-8}^{{sin}^{2}⁡z}{\\int }_{-2y-1}^{{y}^{2}+2z}f(x,y,z)\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=0+\\pi =\\pi .\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161566/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a22ed84a-4b6f-53b3-8336-bf592aed8686"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161566"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161563/selection/cbe428107d005dcdd5e45f88c3988ae1ea4657a311c7f11226ec0e01c270adb8" :answer/id #uuid "f1519679-dfcf-5e0e-95f8-2f0071168365" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2y+8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161563/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "8ce5d283-2b53-5584-b58e-605c9ec84740" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161563/selection/65bc483b0121afa02edfc29250a5c538117e005e49e1f7bb9cc6c69c9f557e17" :answer/id #uuid "b0fc01a3-79f2-52f8-aaf4-4bf5c2cdbf85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{z}^{2}-{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161563/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "c0da0498-6009-583b-a739-a3b823bfe474" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161563/selection/e9952f27731100f28ac8514a475768d1a211e11774bd67ca9b77c680b8f3d452" :answer/id #uuid "069a7d4d-2ef7-5a82-aed4-b61b50f08be6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2y+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161563/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6d9b4dcc-8dfb-5857-bf6a-c65f904912c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161563/selection/cbe428107d005dcdd5e45f88c3988ae1ea4657a311c7f11226ec0e01c270adb8" :answer-field/choices ["q-161563/selection/cbe428107d005dcdd5e45f88c3988ae1ea4657a311c7f11226ec0e01c270adb8" "q-161563/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-161563/selection/65bc483b0121afa02edfc29250a5c538117e005e49e1f7bb9cc6c69c9f557e17" "q-161563/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-161563/selection/e9952f27731100f28ac8514a475768d1a211e11774bd67ca9b77c680b8f3d452"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161563" :question/id #uuid "8bf1bbf2-7733-5ac2-a5df-579136f67cb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-161563" :question/problem "The triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy\n$$\n\nis defined over the type II region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,2y\\le z\\le 8,\\,0\\le x\\le {z}^{2}-{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWhat is $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "A type II region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {u}_{2}(y,z)}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/a905e1f60fb0aa865c071fcbccbfecb30dcac7a74b4b647d24a40f4c89ff1935.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type II region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(y,z)=0,\\,{u}_{2}(y,z)={z}^{2}-{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{{z}^{2}-{y}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA.\n$$\n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,2y\\le z\\le 8}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{{z}^{2}-{y}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{2y}^{8}[{\\int }_{0}^{{z}^{2}-{y}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dz\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{2y}^{8}{\\int }_{0}^{{z}^{2}-{y}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=2y+8.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161563/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a22ed84a-4b6f-53b3-8336-bf592aed8686"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161563"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161548/selection/4fe8b51c91e38ede6c8229c3df9848fc51357a6c8a882af2c29b0768b3180655" :answer/id #uuid "f91ca9ec-5968-5811-96ee-d3283eddcc14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-3}^{5{y}^{4}+2}f(x,y,z)\\,dz]dA" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161548/selection/1ba22a0b814479c1e0601042f885c833a011bffcac98ccf34d97cc1ce66a061f" :answer/id #uuid "32daf30e-1fd3-5377-9c73-44580b3d79d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-3}^{5{y}^{4}+2}[{∬}_{D}f(x,y,z)\\,dA]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161548/selection/01ac07447161752db451d61e29da34cd767d96f2130e85c6cc85c11c69b02b0c" :answer/id #uuid "7da49eb5-2c4b-5895-b48e-9a2f0dc66a43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-3}^{5{y}^{4}+2}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161548/selection/10b219d5a59dd54eee5eb2455bf30e8ef6d66b9a1fc1873510e658460ccc6fa3" :answer/id #uuid "cd74baa0-144c-5982-8e6f-741425d9f5d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-3}^{5{y}^{4}+2}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161548/selection/add9af686fe064e27a498a4c839013bfae77123ba407986059f5b99b82fdcafd" :answer/id #uuid "e7863a08-121e-54d6-b8fd-c1c927175956" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-3}^{5{y}^{4}+2}[{∬}_{D}f(x,y,z)\\,dA]dz" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161548/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b19b6d60-39d9-557f-a2b7-ff61f1e45fea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161548/selection/10b219d5a59dd54eee5eb2455bf30e8ef6d66b9a1fc1873510e658460ccc6fa3" :answer-field/choices ["q-161548/selection/4fe8b51c91e38ede6c8229c3df9848fc51357a6c8a882af2c29b0768b3180655" "q-161548/selection/1ba22a0b814479c1e0601042f885c833a011bffcac98ccf34d97cc1ce66a061f" "q-161548/selection/01ac07447161752db451d61e29da34cd767d96f2130e85c6cc85c11c69b02b0c" "q-161548/selection/10b219d5a59dd54eee5eb2455bf30e8ef6d66b9a1fc1873510e658460ccc6fa3" "q-161548/selection/add9af686fe064e27a498a4c839013bfae77123ba407986059f5b99b82fdcafd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161548" :question/id #uuid "625feabe-c8f9-55d8-bf51-32aafcb00a8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-161548" :question/problem "Consider the type II region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,-3\\le x\\le 5{y}^{4}+2},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is some finite region in the $yz$-plane. Then,\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A type II region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {u}_{2}(y,z)}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/1b49704bf6d5837a18d8b5dbb8b420d430d5e3881507540fb62a45cf1f6ce52f.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type II region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(y,z)=-3\\,{u}_{2}(y,z)=5{y}^{4}+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-3}^{5{y}^{4}+2}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161548/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a22ed84a-4b6f-53b3-8336-bf592aed8686"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161548"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161564/selection/5172fc96a887ebda49e93fb4b460309fd14d1108843860662074151dc8626a8d" :answer/id #uuid "2111342a-b606-54b5-a86e-fce6f1046809" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4-\\sqrt{y+z}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161564/selection/d2a41b50ea09afd996dba4fed4cf0fa7e93b5889fb586323c289e2b04e517419" :answer/id #uuid "831ffbb3-65a6-581f-be22-8a37de7b8634" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161564/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "8e59a877-7829-5aa5-b8de-39ab9aec25e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161564/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "27b5d1f3-ee0f-56e9-88e7-94ed56436816" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161564/selection/690a72aad9c44820eba593eba8d6eff4c80d8fbcdb45e6d87df79d4c87bfae07" :answer/id #uuid "80b554f3-044f-5a61-92d5-63dd1178435f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4+\\sqrt{y+z}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161564/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf378297-4efc-59da-9476-d79c43e94ceb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161564/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer-field/choices ["q-161564/selection/5172fc96a887ebda49e93fb4b460309fd14d1108843860662074151dc8626a8d" "q-161564/selection/d2a41b50ea09afd996dba4fed4cf0fa7e93b5889fb586323c289e2b04e517419" "q-161564/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-161564/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-161564/selection/690a72aad9c44820eba593eba8d6eff4c80d8fbcdb45e6d87df79d4c87bfae07"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161564" :question/id #uuid "0d1c0425-d74e-54e3-8f7e-dc33ee94df6c" :question/math-academy-id "q-161564" :question/problem "The triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz\n$$\n\nis defined over the type II region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-z\\le y\\le 1,\\,4\\le z\\le 5,\\,-\\sqrt{y+z}\\le x\\le 4}.\n$$\n\nWhat is $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "A type II region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {u}_{2}(y,z)}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/a905e1f60fb0aa865c071fcbccbfecb30dcac7a74b4b647d24a40f4c89ff1935.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type II region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(y,z)=-\\sqrt{y+z},\\,{u}_{2}(y,z)=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y+z}}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA.\n$$\n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-z\\le y\\le 1,\\,4\\le z\\le 5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y+z}}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA & ={\\int }_{4}^{5}{\\int }_{-z}^{1}[{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y+z}}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dy\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{4}^{5}{\\int }_{-z}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y+z}}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=4+5=9.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161564/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a22ed84a-4b6f-53b3-8336-bf592aed8686"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161564"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161545/selection/73986a9b61496710d6d79cdf0a2828af5b44321f9458f0524ba72f4ff2b17295" :answer/id #uuid "bb7359d7-c41c-510d-9c53-b2694b769ebe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{yz}^{4}[{∬}_{D}f(x,y,z)\\,dA]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161545/selection/711054db18184aaafaded62330c7e7402d56acb209553c10082dc8e89372b32c" :answer/id #uuid "ffaaf56c-f7f4-57da-806d-dc61326cb39b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{yz}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,dz]dA" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161545/selection/ca5e7421042d8d75ebca9f1aa4afbea14ca42f167b1b36487ee54229e2a42679" :answer/id #uuid "0454310d-f20c-5520-be0b-e0a39b2bbaa1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{yz}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161545/selection/bc3b45bad941262a8fe7705be60d70b7658cc0789fbb67c0f143a718d07203bc" :answer/id #uuid "8507c09c-eabf-5b6d-be58-d771365a0529" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{yz}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161545/selection/db0762716e925b74675ac8fe03ae9ee1b20a46159375ff392ec5c7ba3ccfc77f" :answer/id #uuid "754468a8-049d-540c-b24b-1964c5fea1bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{yz}^{4}[{∬}_{D}f(x,y,z)\\,dA]dy" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161545/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e8311714-cfc5-518b-b248-b0613bcb14f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161545/selection/ca5e7421042d8d75ebca9f1aa4afbea14ca42f167b1b36487ee54229e2a42679" :answer-field/choices ["q-161545/selection/73986a9b61496710d6d79cdf0a2828af5b44321f9458f0524ba72f4ff2b17295" "q-161545/selection/711054db18184aaafaded62330c7e7402d56acb209553c10082dc8e89372b32c" "q-161545/selection/ca5e7421042d8d75ebca9f1aa4afbea14ca42f167b1b36487ee54229e2a42679" "q-161545/selection/bc3b45bad941262a8fe7705be60d70b7658cc0789fbb67c0f143a718d07203bc" "q-161545/selection/db0762716e925b74675ac8fe03ae9ee1b20a46159375ff392ec5c7ba3ccfc77f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161545" :question/id #uuid "283fbbb8-94f0-5ba7-a1c7-86d8e2c0f6e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-161545" :question/problem "Consider the type II region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,yz\\le x\\le 4},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is some finite region in the $yz$-plane. Then,\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A type II region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {u}_{2}(y,z)}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063435/assets/1b49704bf6d5837a18d8b5dbb8b420d430d5e3881507540fb62a45cf1f6ce52f.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type II region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(y,z)=yz\\,{u}_{2}(y,z)=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{yz}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161545/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a22ed84a-4b6f-53b3-8336-bf592aed8686"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161545"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-40395"] :question/problem "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y}12z\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 4-{y}^{2}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y}12z\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}12z[x]_{x=0}^{x=y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}12z(y-0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}12yz\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}yz\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4-{y}^{2}}12yz\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}6y[{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=4-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}6y(4-{y}^{2})^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(96y-48{y}^{3}+6{y}^{5})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[48{y}^{2}-12{y}^{4}+{y}^{6}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =48(2)^{2}-12(2)^{4}+(2)^{6} \\\\  & =64\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-161560/selection/16ad0c2afac2310ac4213e4c147a8ff875d80d039203f9a4d0bd13914017aaff" :answer/id #uuid "855588bd-17c6-5cb3-905b-eea06e2c2a66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "104" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161560/selection/71ec7720d7077a8c88c1c4a9c53a3f81078793450c23aec02efcc43f1fc689b6" :answer/id #uuid "99da2280-53f2-5e5b-b72d-02dcf3fa4b49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "82" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161560/selection/efc1f4b9a49230e3a3d3e4045f87c921d5c73534634163a59bc9f874eec80485" :answer/id #uuid "0f4f2f4e-5fde-56ef-b4db-a58c33a6f28a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "124" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161560/selection/09269df15e3fb141cceebb0588aab82a40ef42df1a8a11f4146bedfe71482238" :answer/id #uuid "83fc4178-3778-561f-a894-30026f919f85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "94" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161560/selection/7ba4ebd0d8a414ae4c404538d01dce67a31f8f6714da9cff2a89b3a7ecb90e95" :answer/id #uuid "e3437526-8df8-5c32-8411-217b35638a43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "76" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161560/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8f29b384-fa33-5b83-9cd5-e308d52b498a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161560/selection/16ad0c2afac2310ac4213e4c147a8ff875d80d039203f9a4d0bd13914017aaff" :answer-field/choices ["q-161560/selection/16ad0c2afac2310ac4213e4c147a8ff875d80d039203f9a4d0bd13914017aaff" "q-161560/selection/71ec7720d7077a8c88c1c4a9c53a3f81078793450c23aec02efcc43f1fc689b6" "q-161560/selection/efc1f4b9a49230e3a3d3e4045f87c921d5c73534634163a59bc9f874eec80485" "q-161560/selection/09269df15e3fb141cceebb0588aab82a40ef42df1a8a11f4146bedfe71482238" "q-161560/selection/7ba4ebd0d8a414ae4c404538d01dce67a31f8f6714da9cff2a89b3a7ecb90e95"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161560" :question/id #uuid "e407a798-2ab7-5ae6-bcb2-5c2001782993" :question/math-academy-id "q-161560" :question/problem "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y+2z}2\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,0\\le z\\le 2y}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y+2z}2\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}2[x]_{x=0}^{x=y+2z}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2(y+2z-0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2y+4z\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2y+4z\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2y}2y+4z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}[2yz+2{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=2y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}2y(2y)+2(2y)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}4{y}^{2}+8{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}12{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[4{y}^{3}]_{y=1}^{y=3} \\\\  & =4(27-1) \\\\  & =104\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :questi